From e313d0e4f19da6a9e1c8442a84c24973c4028803 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:37:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] test(ci): prove login-session routing by lane
 collection, not source

Review 5911661283 (P2): the AST inventory read test source, which tests/AGENTS.md bans, and it
missed the selector prerequisite. Dropping platforms("posix") from the snapshot-restore test
left all 30 workflow tests green while list_os_marked_tests.py macos stopped importing the file.

The new test runs each lane's real file selector and -m expression from macos-os-tests.yml,
then has pytest collect the three files. The session lane must select exactly the five cases
and the room lane none of them. --strict-markers keeps the marker-registration check behavioral.

Proof (MacBook, hermes-core-wt test --local; predictions written first, all held): 30 passed.
- Reviewer's mutant (platforms("posix") dropped): survives the old file (30 passed) but fails the
  new test.
- The six earlier mutants stay killed:
  - each omitted function marker fails the new test;
  - GUI preflight fail-open fails both GUI-domain cases;
  - room exclusion removal fails the new test and the room job shape test;
  - session selector broadening fails the new test and both GUI-domain cases.
- Unregistering the marker fails the new test (collection error).
- The new test takes 2.5-5.1 s.
---
